From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:28:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: mediatek: drop the transceiver before its device
 goes

The glue registers a generic USB PHY device, takes it as its transceiver
with devm_usb_get_phy(), and unregisters the device by hand in remove and
on probe errors. The device's unbind frees the usb_phy, and devres then
puts the transceiver from freed memory. Unloading the module on a Gemini
PDA oopsed in usb_put_phy(), called from devm_usb_phy_release() during
driver detach.

Take the transceiver with usb_get_phy() and put it before unregistering
the generic PHY device, in remove and on the probe error paths after it.
---
 drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
index 152d8c0b8..9b0cab801 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
@@ -517,7 +517,11 @@ static int mtk_musb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(glue->usb_phy),
 				"fail to registering usb-phy\n");
 
-	glue->xceiv = devm_usb_get_phy(dev, USB_PHY_TYPE_USB2);
+	/*
+	 * Not devm: the reference must go before the generic PHY device it
+	 * points into is unregistered, which remove does by hand.
+	 */
+	glue->xceiv = usb_get_phy(USB_PHY_TYPE_USB2);
 	if (IS_ERR(glue->xceiv)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(glue->xceiv);
 		dev_err(dev, "fail to getting usb-phy %d\n", ret);
@@ -555,6 +559,7 @@ static int mtk_musb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 err_enable_clk:
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	usb_put_phy(glue->xceiv);
 err_unregister_usb_phy:
 	usb_phy_generic_unregister(glue->usb_phy);
 	return ret;
@@ -566,6 +571,7 @@ static void mtk_musb_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct platform_device *usb_phy = glue->usb_phy;
 
 	platform_device_unregister(glue->musb_pdev);
+	usb_put_phy(glue->xceiv);
 	usb_phy_generic_unregister(usb_phy);
 }
 
